cff-version: 1.2.0
title: AI Character Index
message: >-
  This file cites the software in this repository. The index's data is not
  in this repository: it is served by the site, and each publication has an
  identifier and a date. To cite the data, use the citation the site gives
  for the publication you read, at
  https://ai-character-index.vercel.app/how-it-works. The specifications the
  index reads are third-party works and should be cited to their own
  publishers, not to this project.
type: software

# Andrés Cotton and Matt Stults created the index and its method (the rubric,
# the scale, the prompt and the citation grammar, referenced below) and wrote
# most of the behaviour briefs. Polaris Collective maintains this fork, its
# deployment, its judging job and its portal.
authors:
  - given-names: Andrés
    family-names: Cotton
  - given-names: Matt
    family-names: Stults
  - name: Polaris Collective
    website: 'https://polariscollective.org'

contact:
  - name: Polaris Collective
    website: 'https://polariscollective.org'

abstract: >-
  The software behind a structured index of where published AI behaviour
  specifications address particular model behaviours: a panel of LLM judges
  reads each specification whole, marks the passages that bear on each
  behaviour and gives the document a 0 to 4 depth, and every citation is
  recorded with a locator resolving to verbatim spec text. It includes the
  judging job, the publication builder and verifier, the reader, the admin
  portal and the MCP server.

# This fork. The original stands alone and is the one to clone to run the
# tool from a bare checkout: https://github.com/AndresCotton/ai-character-index
repository-code: 'https://github.com/polariscollective/ai-character-index'
url: 'https://ai-character-index.vercel.app/spec-reader/'
license:
  - Apache-2.0
  - CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - AI alignment
  - model specifications
  - behaviour coverage
  - LLM evaluation

# The original and its method, credited on their own line.
references:
  - type: software
    title: AI Character Index
    abstract: >-
      The original, standalone AI Character Index, and the method this index
      runs: the depth rubric and its scale, the judging prompt and the
      citation grammar.
    authors:
      - given-names: Andrés
        family-names: Cotton
      - given-names: Matt
        family-names: Stults
    repository-code: 'https://github.com/AndresCotton/ai-character-index'
    url: 'https://ai-character-index.pages.dev'
